AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::setIrm()
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
├── when new IRM is zero address
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress before accruing interest
├── when new IRM equals current IRM
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput before accruing interest
├── when new IRM does not report FIXED_RATE
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput before accruing interest
├── when new IRM type query reverts or returns malformed data
│   └── it should propagate the failure and preserve current IRM
├── given skipAccrueInterest is false
│   ├── when market is not paused
│   │   ├── it should accrue interest using the old IRM before updating the address
│   │   └── it should preserve current IRM when old IRM accrual fails
│   └── when market is paused
│       └── it should skip old IRM accrual
├── given skipAccrueInterest is true
│   └── it should skip old IRM accrual whether market is active paused or frozen
├── given a valid new fixed-rate IRM
│   ├── it should emit SetIrm with old and new addresses after optional accrual
│   ├── it should update irm
│   ├── it should call setMarket on the new IRM with the credit line address
│   ├── when new IRM rejects market registration
│   │   └── it should revert and restore old IRM and accrued state
│   └── it should reject and roll back a reentrant call
└── when market is frozen but not paused and accrual is not skipped
    └── it should still accrue using the old IRM
